### Phase 6: Package Strategy

- [x] Decide whether to create `packages/shared`, `packages/core`, or keep `src/shared` first.
- [x] If monorepo is deferred, create migration-safe aliases.
- [x] If monorepo starts, configure build/typecheck incrementally.
- [x] Keep the current app deployable after every extraction.

Package strategy:

- Keep the current single Next.js app and npm/package-lock install contract.
- Defer `packages/shared`, `packages/core`, pnpm, and Turbo until route/module/data boundaries are stable and pilot flows remain deployable.
- Use `src/shared`, `src/app-shell`, `src/features`, and `src/server` as the near-term package-like boundaries.

Migration-safe aliases:

- Added `@app-shell/*` for `src/app-shell/*`.
- Added `@features/*` for `src/features/*`.
- Added `@server/*` for `src/server/*`.
- Added `@shared/*` for `src/shared/*`.
- Added matching Next webpack/Turbopack aliases.
- Added `src/shared/index.ts` as the shared boundary barrel.

Future extraction rule:

- Only extract a folder into `packages/*` after its imports already use the boundary alias and `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`, and Supabase contract checks pass.
- Keep `npm` until package extraction creates enough value to justify a package-manager migration.

