### Phase 7: API Strategy

- [x] Classify APIs as browser-Supabase, server route, RPC, edge function, or future service.
- [x] Move sensitive writes behind server/RPC boundaries.
- [x] Define idempotent mutation conventions.
- [x] Define audit logging requirements.

API strategy:

- Added `src/server/api-boundary.ts` with API boundary kinds, security levels, mutation policies, current boundary definitions, service-role write rules, and idempotent mutation rules.
- Classified feature repositories as browser Supabase/RLS operations.
- Classified onboarding, employee invites, cron jobs, and detectors as Next route handler boundaries.
- Classified company setup/invite database helpers as Supabase RPC boundaries.
- Classified AI/copilot/learning/schedule/vendor functions as Supabase edge-function boundaries that require auth, tenant checks, CORS tightening, idempotency, and audit/event logging before production enablement.
- Classified external integration orchestration as a future service boundary.

Sensitive write hardening:

- Moved employee email invites out of the client component and behind `app/api/employees/invite/route.ts`.
- The invite route verifies the bearer session server-side, resolves company/role server-side, writes/updates the invite record idempotently, sends the Supabase invite using service role, and writes an `audit_log` entry.
- Updated `src/features/employees/components/InviteEmployeePanel.tsx` to call the server route instead of `supabase.auth.admin`.

Verification:

- Service-role leakage scan found no client-side `supabase.auth.admin` or service-role references outside server routes/server code.
- `npm run typecheck` passed.
- `npm run build` passed.
- `npm run check:supabase` passed.

Acceptance:

